This repository contains a public case study: written material, page markup and
styling, diagrams, and screenshots describing the Rahzaan academic career-guidance
system. It is published so the work can be read and assessed. It is not published
for reuse.

No licence, express or implied, is granted to any person to copy, modify, merge,
publish, distribute, sublicense, or sell any part of the contents of this
repository, or to create derivative works from it. The absence of an open-source
licence here is deliberate and is not an oversight.

The Rahzaan system itself, including its source code, its curated admission and
eligibility data, its derived rules, and its assessment materials, is not
contained in this repository and is separately owned. Rahzaan was built by
Muhammad Waqas Sharif as primary author and lead developer, with design
contribution from Muhammad Khuzaim Sajjad and data contribution from Fazal ur
Rehman Khan.

Quoting short passages for commentary, review, reporting, teaching, or
scholarship, with attribution, is expected and welcome. Reproducing the case
study in substantial part, or reusing the page design or screenshots, is not.

For any other permission, contact ma.sharif.waqas@gmail.com.
